What is a Terraform Provider and why is it important?
Can you also give a real-world example of using a provider in a cloud project?


A Terraform Provider is a plugin that lets Terraform talk to a specific cloud or service (like AWS, GCP, Azure, Kubernetes, GitHub, etc.).
 It knows how to create, read, update, and delete the resources for that service.
When you run terraform init, Terraform downloads the required provider plugin from the Terraform Registry.

Real-World Example:
 If you want to create a VM in Google Cloud, you use the Google Provider:

provider "google" {
 project = "my-project-id"
 region = "us-central1"
}


This provider knows how to create Compute Engine VMs, Cloud Storage Buckets, SQL Databases, etc., in GCP.
Without the provider, Terraform wouldn’t know how to talk to GCP
